/*--------------------------------------------
A convex mirror with a focusing lens and a screen (a small catadioptric system).

Light from a point source meets a convex mirror (R = 200 mm, so f = -100 mm). The mirror sends it back,
diverging, as if from a small virtual image behind the mirror. A plus lens (f = 150 mm) in the reflected
beam then brings it to a real image, and the screen sits there.

After the mirror the light travels the other way, so the medium is written with a NEGATIVE index (-1, the
usual reflection convention) and the distances that follow are NEGATIVE: the lens is 250 mm to the
left of the mirror, the screen 275 mm further left.
----------------------------------------------*/
